# EqInputCat
# TilingCat
# v46
# 2015-05-22
# Ivan Baldry <i.baldry@ljmu.ac.uk>
#
# Science targets in the GAMA II equatorial survey regions.
# 
CATAID             1  -             meta.id;meta.main            Unique GAMA ID of object
OBJID              2  -             meta.id                      SDSS objid
RA                 3  deg           pos.eq.ra                    J2000 coordinate
DEC                4  deg           pos.eq.dec                   J2000 coordinate
FIBERMAG_R         5  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.R            SDSS DR7 r band fibre magnitude
R_PETRO            6  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.R            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 r band Petrosian magnitude 
U_MODEL            7  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.U            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 u band model magnitude
G_MODEL            8  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.B            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 g band model magnitude
R_MODEL            9  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.R            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 r band model magnitude
I_MODEL           10  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.I            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 i band model magnitude
Z_MODEL           11  mag           phot.mag;em.opt.I            Extinction-corrected SDSS DR7 z band model magnitude
SURVEY_CODE       12  -             meta.code;meta.dataset       Survey code for redshift source, see notes
Z                 13  -             src.redshift                 Spectroscopic redshift, -1 for none attempted
NQ                14  -             meta.code.qual;src.redshift  Quality of redshift
NQ2_FLAG          15  -             meta.code.qual;src.redshift  Tests of NQ=2 redshifts, see notes
SPECID            16  -             meta.id.cross;spect          ID of spectrum from SpecAll table
VEL_ERR           17  km/s          src.redshift;stat.error      Redshift uncertainty, c delta ln(1+z), see notes
NUM_GAMA_SPEC     18  -             meta.number;spect            Number of GAMA spectra within 1 arcsec
R_SB              19  mag/arcsec^2  phot.mag.sb;em.opt.R         SDSS Petro half-light surface brightness
SG_SEP            20  mag           src.class.starGalaxy         r_psf - r_model star-galaxy separation parameter
SG_SEP_JK         21  mag           src.class.starGalaxy         J - K - f_locus star-galaxy separation parameter
K_AUTO            22  mag           phot.mag;em.IR.K             Extinction-corrected r-defined auto AB mag 
RADIO_FLUX        23  mJy           phot.flux.density;em.radio   Flux from FIRST-SDSS matching
HATLAS_FLAG       24  -             meta.code                    1 for match to H-ATLAS SDSS possible ID
AREA_FLAG         25  -             meta.code                    1-deg strip, 2 for GAMA I regions
TARGET_FLAGS      26  -             meta.code                    Bitwise target criteria, see notes
SURVEY_OLDCLASS   27  -             meta.code.class              Useful for selecting samples, see notes
SURVEY_CLASS      28  -             meta.code.class              Useful for selecting samples, see notes
PRIORITY_CLASS    29  -             meta.code.class              Priorities for targeting, see notes
NEIGHBOUR_CLASS   30  -             meta.code.class              Number of survey_class>=3 targets within 40 arcsec
TC_V11_ID         31  -             meta.code.cross              CATAID of object in TilingCatv11, see notes
MASK_IC_10        32  -             meta.code                    Mask value 0.0 to 1.0 around V<10 stars
MASK_IC_12        33  -             meta.code                    Mask value 0.0 to 1.0 around V<12 stars
VIS_CLASS         34  -             mata.code.qual               Visual classification, see notes
VIS_CLASS_USER    35  -             meta.id                      Initials of classifiers, xxx for none
